00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:26.900
Maybe.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:27.600
Hellow.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:28.820
Aaaaahhhh.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.160
See, I'm really glad that I kinda branched out back into doing these indie horror games,

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.820
because number one, you never know what you're gonna get.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.060
I mean, a lot of these indie horror games, they kinda go on the jumpscare trope,

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.420
but, occasionally, you'll come across an interesting little game

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.160
that has a, y'know, it has a premise,

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.500
and it has, a story,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:49.880
and it has an environment.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.100
These are all generic things that I'm saying, but I'm trying to...

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.120
be intellectual about what I'm saying

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.800
but you never know what you're gonna get  once you go into it

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.100
so you can see-

00:01:59.100 --> 00:01:59.600
